WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.630
In the same way that you have to grasp the
Kents to know Superman, there's no wrapping

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.210
your head around Wonder Woman without a firm
understanding of the isolated island where

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.560
she grew up.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.340
Without the lessons she learned in her matriarchal
society, there is no Wonder Woman.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.060
This is the history of Themyscira, explained

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.180
Before diving into Wonder Woman's history
on Themyscira, it's worth understanding why

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.550
she was created in the first place.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.420
Where many years of fan service from the entertainment
industry might lead you to believe that Wonder

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:35.469
Woman was a cash grab to capitalize on young
girls who weren't buying Golden Age comics,

00:00:35.469 --> 00:00:39.040
the real origin of the character is considerably
more idealistic.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.500
"Don't you think it's time to start my training?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.489
Antiope thinks I'm ready!"

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:51.359
As the 2017 film Professor Marston &amp; the Wonder
Women depicts, William Moulton Marston created

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:56.199
the character to put forward the idea of a
feminist utopia, believing that a world led

00:00:56.199 --> 00:00:59.670
by women with the interests of women first
would be a better one.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.730
The inventor and psychologist exaggerated
the traits of the liberated women he saw around

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.690
him, especially the two women he was in a
polyamorous relationship with, and created

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.460
a new kind of hero.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.040
Marston wrote in The American Scholar about
his most famous creation,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.670
"Not even girls want to be girls so long as
our feminine archetype lacks force, strength,

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:21.670
and power.

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.190
Not wanting to be girls, they don't want to
be tender, submissive, peace-loving as good

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.240
women are.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.970
Women's strong qualities have become despised
because of their weakness.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.640
The obvious remedy is to create a feminine
character with all the strength of Superman

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.980
plus all the allure of a good and beautiful
woman."

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.250
For the moral of Wonder Woman to land, she
couldn't be an anomaly in her world.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.330
She had to come from an entire nation of powerful
women, whose world proved Marston's thesis

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.110
of a better world built entirely by women.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.500
In short, Themyscira needed to be a paradise.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.240
Marston, who used pen name Charles Moulton,
wrote at the time,

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:03.659
"Wonder Woman is psychological propaganda
for the new type of woman who should, I believe,

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:04.659
rule the world."

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.830
And so Wonder Woman's home was designed as
an idyllic paradise, almost comically so.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.620
The original name of Themyscira — in that
uniquely plainspoken language of Golden Age

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.189
comics — was Paradise Island.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:22.690
Early issues made it very clear what they
wanted readers to take away from the island

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.690
overall.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:28.030
It was a perfect place — and it was perfect
because of the exclusion of men.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.279
Other names floated during the early years
of Wonder Woman were equally descriptive.

00:02:32.279 --> 00:02:38.079
The island was known as the Amazon Isles,
because of its status as home of the Amazons.

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:43.510
Occasionally it was known as Paradise Isle,
for reasons that are just as easy to guess.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:49.290
It didn't take on its name of Themyscira until
decades after Wonder Woman first graced the

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:50.290
page.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:54.900
The island of Themyscira came into existence
in the fallout from the massive DC crossover

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.150
event Crisis on Infinite Earths in the '80s.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.349
The landmark event was a way to cast off decades
of canon and continuity, streamlining the

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:07.560
DC universe under a series of new titles with
clear backstories.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.469
So it was that Paradise Island became Themyscira.

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:17.299
According to the post-reboot continuity, Themyscira
didn't begin its life as an island at all.

00:03:17.299 --> 00:03:21.359
Instead it was a city-state of Amazons near
modern-day Turkey.

00:03:21.359 --> 00:03:26.540
The state was created by the gods themselves,
molding the Amazons out of clay and tasking

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.989
them with teaching traits like compassion
to the wider world.

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:34.279
From the beginning of their time on Earth,
the Amazons are depicted as being in contention

00:03:34.279 --> 00:03:36.639
with Ares, the God of War.

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:42.389
As the Amazons spread ideas like good will
and world peace, Ares corrupts humanity and

00:03:42.389 --> 00:03:44.639
steers them toward vengeance and anger.

00:03:44.639 --> 00:03:49.939
They square off with their bitter rival wherever
they find him trying to steer the wider world

00:03:49.939 --> 00:03:54.809
toward destruction and they model their virtues
in their own city-state, which is known to

00:03:54.809 --> 00:03:56.189
be a paradise.

00:03:56.189 --> 00:04:02.400
The state of Themyscira is ruled over by Hippolyta
and Antiope, monarchs and sisters.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:09.139
Ares eventually disrupts the idyllic capital
of the Amazons by tricking Heracles, aka Hercules,

00:04:09.139 --> 00:04:11.030
into attacking the Amazons.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:16.199
His initial attack is unsuccessful, as the
extremely powerful Amazons quickly defeat

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:17.199
him.

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:22.090
Hippolyta and Antiope live in a society that
is largely free of rage and deceit, one that's

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.780
built on forgiveness.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:28.770
Because of this, they invite the humiliated
Hercules to a feast in their capital to embark

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.170
on a new era of friendship.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.010
Hercules has other things in mind, however.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:39.130
He attends the feast as a ruse to get his
forces inside the city without resistance.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.910
At the feast, he drugs the Amazons and takes
them prisoner.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:48.670
The Amazons plead to the women of Mount Olympus
and Athena finally responds to their cries,

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:52.880
offering to free them from bondage if they
agree not to seek revenge on the men who had

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.290
enslaved them.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:59.500
Because Athena's goal is to foster creation,
she views all destruction of life as evil.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:04.200
The Amazons agree, though not all among them
actually hold feelings of forgiveness in their

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.440
hearts: Athena uses her powers to break the
chains holding the Amazons captive — and

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.100
many of them proceed to slaughter the men
who had held them.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.200
This angers Athena, and she comes down hard
on the Amazons, demanding that they pay penance

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.720
for what they've done and sending them to
an island — one they name after their former

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.620
capital — that sits on top of the doorway
to the underworld.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:31.390
Their role as guardians helps to pay back
Athena by keeping destructive forces out of

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.580
the world of man.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:37.270
In addition, the Amazons have to wear bracelets
as reminders of the time they were tricked

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.630
into slavery.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:42.180
Not all of them are entirely willing to go
along with the plan, though.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:46.610
These "bracelets of submission" are symbols
of their devotion to the goddess Aphrodite

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:50.180
and reminders of what waited for them outside
of their island.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:55.280
The Amazon warriors were raised from birth
to view falling prisoner to a man as the gravest

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.620
possible outcome.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:01.770
The iconic gold bands were a symbol of real-world
women's status in society and the hope that

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.170
they would break out of oppressive systems.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:08.190
The bracelets also had quite a bit to do with
Marston's own affinity for bondage.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.870
Though Hippolyta and Antiope had ruled as
co-leaders of the Amazons since time immemorial,

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:20.280
the decision to retreat from the world of
man and set up a peace-loving society on Themyscira

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.670
doesn't sit right with one of them.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:27.870
Antiope disavows her fellow Amazons, taking
with her a force of vengeful warriors who

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:31.860
are entirely unwilling to forgive the men
who had enslaved them.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.210
Antiope sets out to destroy Hercules and his
general Theseus.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.910
Though she does not get her revenge, she ends
up falling in love with Theseus and starting

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:41.910
a family.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:46.300
The exiled Amazons try to make peace with
the Greek forces of Theseus, but most of them

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:51.240
can't countenance fighting alongside the same
men who invaded and enslaved them.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:56.840
Antiope is eventually killed by the vengeful
ex-wife of Theseus, breaking the tenuous alliance

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:00.320
between Theseus' army and the band of Amazons.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:05.020
The remaining Amazons promote Antiope's adopted
daughter to be their leader, and they head

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.930
out to a remote corner of the Earth.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:11.770
They set up shop in the deep desert of the
Middle East, creating a colony while Themyscira

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.350
carries on outside the world of man.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:19.550
Though Themyscira is meant to be an island
fortress separate from man's world, that would

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:22.370
make for a remarkably boring story.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:27.330
Over the years, many intruders have landed
on the island's shores, both intentionally

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.730
and accidentally.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:34.030
Everyone from random fighter pilots to Darkseid
have made their way to Themyscira over the

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.030
years.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:39.250
The cosmic villain invaded the island and
wiped out half of its population.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.110
Hercules tried yet again to subdue the Amazons.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:46.970
Aliens have invaded from deep within the recesses
of Jack Kirby's mind.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:51.380
The goddess Hera has invaded, turning all
but the queen into snakes.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:56.370
They've frequently been turned to stone, aesthetically
in line with their classical Greek island.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:01.150
But because of the slippery nature of comic
book continuity, where death rarely lasts,

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:06.650
and the enduring passion of the Amazons, Themyscira
always returns in some form or fashion.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:12.770
All this history and ancient intrigue leads
us to the rather odd birth of a classic DC

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:13.770
superhero.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:18.380
Hippolyta formed her daughter Diana, who we
come to know as Wonder Woman, from the dirt

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:19.930
of the island of Themyscira.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.300
"Hello, Mother.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.040
How are you today?"

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:29.220
Destined to bring change to her native land,
Diana objects to the isolation of Themyscira

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:33.210
— and she eventually comes to serve as an
ambassador between the necessarily sheltered

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:37.669
world of superpowered women where she came
into being and the world of man.

00:08:37.669 --> 00:08:43.090
Diana's sway in both worlds leads to an era
of open borders, with visitors from the outside

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:48.310
world stopping by with the welcome of the
royal family for the first time in eons.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:52.680
As Diana becomes one of the protectors of
the outside world through her work — both

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:58.110
as a solo superhero and a member of the Justice
League — many dignitaries and representatives

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.740
want to know more about her hidden home.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.030
And why wouldn't they?

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:06.960
These superwomen uphold the ideals of love
and peace in their own society, serving as

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.320
an example to all humanity.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.170
As an extra bit of poetic justice, the Amazons
were crafted out of the souls of women who

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.840
had met violent deaths at the hands of men.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:20.340
"As Amazons, this is our duty!"

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:22.920
